Step 08.7 part 7: budget-aware cascade early-stop runtime dispatch validation
Scope: reuse calibrated 6B routes and observables, then validate a cascade runtime that stops early whenever a cheaper route already looks reliable.
Constraints: no new DOA algorithm, no V2, no complex-gain q, no 4D search, no fullscan, no edits to step 8.6 or prior 8.7 outputs.
Geometry: Q=65, Nel=32, theta_sep=0.263775445 deg.
Run control: Metkl=30, SNR=[0 8 16], T_snap=260, sep_factor=10.
Scenario set is reused from 6B; this part validates runtime structure and estimated cost rather than new boundary coverage.
2D MUSIC K=[20,8], pair-local covfit K=[6,3], refocus_el_grid=29.
Cost model: level2 MUSIC=1, rank1=2, refocus=2, 2D MUSIC=8, pair-local=10.
Scenario count=51. Groups are reused exactly from 6B: rho scan, beta scan, phase scan, and representative large-el cases.
